# gamified3D overview

Game-style 3D / 2.5D scenes for the web on three.js. Companion to gamifiedUI
(c:\Users\kason\Desktop\gamifiedUI): gamifiedUI owns CSS UI (HUD, panels, icons, CSS-only `gx-iso`
scenes); gamified3D owns anything that needs WebGL. Never put CSS components here, and never put
three.js code in gamifiedUI.

## Layout (npm workspaces)

- `packages/*` - one package per module, each with its own `LICENSE`, `NOTICE` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
- `three` is a peer dependency of every package, never bundled.

## Design contract

- Renderers take state in (actor positions, time of day, weather) and draw it; they hold no game
  logic and do not depend on Phaser or any framework.
- Respect reduced motion: ambient animation (water, smoke, villagers) stops when the host passes
  `isReducedMotion`.
- Palettes default to gamifiedUI's era themes so the HUD and the world match.

## Commands (PowerShell; no `&&` chaining in docs)

- `npm install`.

## Planned packages

- `gamified3d-diorama` - low-poly diorama renderer, ported from StoryTelling
  `frontend/src/game/views/lowPolyView.ts` and `frontend/src/game/lowpoly/*`.
